  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        498.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "On 10 April 1912 the opulent liner Titanic left Southampton on her maiden voyage. A 1911 trade journal had dubbed her and her sister ship \"practically unsinkable\". At about 11.40pm on 14 April she collided with an iceberg; by 2.20am she had vanished beneath the waves, and the death toll would surpass 1,500."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        371.3614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        490.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Folklore blames arrogance. Yet the Titanic was compliant with the law. Under 1894 rules, Britain's maritime regulator pegged lifeboat numbers to gross tonnage (volume, not weight) on a scale that topped out at 16 boats for 10,000 tons or more. At about 46,000 tons she carried 20, exceeding the requirement. Their capacity was 1,178, roughly half the 2,200 aboard: sufficient in law, inadequate at sea."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        263.8614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        362.8614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Within radio range, the steamer Californian kept an equally lawful routine. Her sole wireless operator, Cyril Evans, was on the payroll of the Marconi company; when he slept, so did the radio. Around 11.30pm he switched off his set. Hindsight may call that negligence, yet no rule obliged him to stay vigilant, so the Titanic's frantic distress calls went unheard there."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        136.5614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        255.3614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Between April and July 1912, inquiries in Washington and London heard testimony from survivors and the Californian's crew. That July, American legislation made round-the-clock radio watch compulsory. In January 1914 delegates of 13 nations signed the first Safety of Life at Sea convention, stipulating lifeboat seats for all, continuous radio watch, and an ice patrol. The First World War stalled the treaty; the patrol went ahead regardless."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        88.4614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        128.0614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The doomed liner sank within three hours. The outdated rules she sailed under had stayed afloat since 1894; it took her dead to discredit them."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1912年4月10日，豪华的邮轮泰坦尼克号离开了南安普敦，开始了她的处女航。1911年，一家行业期刊把她和她的姊妹船称为“几乎不会沉没的”。4月14日晚约11时40分，她和一座冰山相撞了；到次日凌晨2时20分，她已消失在海浪之下，遇难人数最终将超过1,500。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        409.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "坊间流传的说法把灾难归咎于傲慢。然而泰坦尼克号符合法规。按照1894年的规则，英国的海事监管机构把救生艇数量与总吨位（体积，而非重量）挂钩，在一个等级表上/等级体系中，（其数量）最高达（只能）到16艘，针对10,000吨及以上（的船）。她约有46,000吨，带了20艘，超出了要求。它们的容量是1,178人，大约是船上2,200人的一半：按法律足够，到了海上却不足。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        300.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        400.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "在无线电通讯范围内，加州人号轮船遵循的是一套同样合法的值班惯例。她唯一的无线电操作员西里尔·埃文斯，受雇于马可尼公司；他一睡下，电台也一样睡了。晚上11时30分左右，他关掉了自己的设备。事后看来，这或许可称为疏忽，然而没有哪条规则强制他保持警觉，所以泰坦尼克号发狂似的求救呼叫，在那里无人听见。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        192.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        292.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "1912年4月至7月，华盛顿和伦敦的调查听取了幸存者以及加州人号船员的证词。同年7月，美国的一项立法将全天候无线电值守定为强制性的（义务）。1914年1月，13国的代表签署了第一部《海上人命安全公约》，规定救生艇座位要够所有人乘坐，电台要不间断值守，还要开展冰情巡逻。第一次世界大战让这项条约暂缓搁置了；然而冰情巡逻不管怎样依然进行。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        143.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        183.66141732283472
      ],
      "text": "这艘在劫难逃的邮轮不到三小时就沉没了。她航行时所遵循的那套过时的规则，却自1894年起一直没有沉没；直到她的乘客葬身大海，它们才信誉扫地。"
    }
  ],
